#N canvas 100 100 700 500 12;
#X obj 40 20 inlet;
#X obj 40 60 route ratio play stop;
#X obj 220 100 f 1;
#X obj 40 140 t b b;
#X obj 40 180 array size $1;
#X obj 40 260 expr ($f1/44100*1000)/$f2;
#X msg 40 300 play 0 $1 44100 \$1 0 0 0 5;
#X msg 320 60 stop 0;
#X obj 40 340 timeStretch~;
#X obj 40 400 outlet~;
#X text 200 20 stem_timestretch~ <arrayname>: wraps William Brent's
timeStretch~ (real phase-vocoder time-stretch \, pitch-independent \,
replaces Max's karma~) with a simple ratio-controlled interface for
BPM-align preview. Send "ratio <f>" to set the stretch ratio (1 =
normal speed \, 2 = double speed/half duration \, 0.5 = half speed/double
duration) BEFORE sending "play". Send "play" to start playback of
the whole buffer at the current ratio (always starts from the beginning
-- this does not support changing ratio smoothly mid-playback \, re-send
"play" to restart at a new ratio). Send "stop" to stop. Voice 0 is
always used (single-voice per stem \, matching the rest of this patch's
one-buffer-per-stem design). Depends on timeStretch~.pd and lib/timestretch-reader-abs.pd
(vendored unmodified from https://github.com/wbrent/timeStretch_tilde
\, GPL-3.0) sitting alongside this abstraction., f 300;
#X connect 0 0 1 0;
#X connect 1 0 2 1;
#X connect 1 1 3 0;
#X connect 1 2 7 0;
#X connect 2 0 5 1;
#X connect 3 0 4 0;
#X connect 3 1 2 0;
#X connect 4 0 5 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 6 0 8 0;
#X connect 7 0 8 0;
#X connect 8 0 9 0;
